[issue.1904]
number = 1904
title = "[Coherence] The disposition of finding 22.33.917.1 says it is resolved, but main no longer binds the reward migration approval, so the production registry is still refused"
revision = "3520b1428059af90261432778c008a9ce362a0b1"
verdict = "spec-edit"
evidence = "Completed closure task 22.39.198 (spec/layerx-merge/spec.kvx:350940,350947,350948) must correct spec/layerx-merge/dispositions/d22-30.kvx:325-328 to mark finding 22.33.917.1 open with a registered follow_up task for reviewed reward migration approval: commit 3924248dd2fc42125eb6f7c5b735d475471e379b supplied the binding, but commit 288ea8df07da84b1ec1b42c7a49fefe47352b9b2 withdrew it, leaving migration 180001 metadata null at launchpad/spec/production-system/integration/migrations/registry.json:2051-2058 and registry approval null at :2591; LoadRewardRegistry calls the shared loader first (services/launchpad/pnl-tracker/internal/migrate/reward.go:14-16), which returns unapproved migration registry through sdk/launchpad/shared/db/production/migrations.go:645 and :232-233 before the reward-specific comparison at reward.go:38-39, so the fresh-install and upgrade cases at services/launchpad/pnl-tracker/internal/app/repair_m917_test.go:37-41 cannot pass their admission check at :57-59; the proposed reader digest, version 1 and 2000ms bound remain in launchpad/spec/production-system/integration/migrations/pnl-reward-approval.json:12-14, while spec/layerx-merge/spec.kvx:361151 and tools/qualification/audit_repairs/test_repair_22_33_815.py:122-154 require refusal until reviewed qualification exists, and the separate schema-description issue #1587 does not resolve this approval gap."
close_comment = "Finding 22.33.917.1 needs an open disposition with current approval-refusal evidence and a registered follow-up for reviewed migration approval; its resolved claim is stale because the production registry no longer binds the reward approval. Production admission must remain refused until the complete registry has the required reviewed evidence, with fresh-install and upgrade coverage proving the approved reward migration."
